<title>UK: Fidelity targets Lloyd's insurance market.</title>
<headline>Fidelity targets Lloyd's insurance market.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-04-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Fidelity Investments said it is targeting managing agents within the Lloyd's of London insurance market with its triple A-rated Institutional Cash Fund.</p>
<p>&quot;Lloyd's is one of the largest cash markets in the UK. Fidelity's Institutional Cash Fund will give managing agents a high yielding and more secure alternative to bank accounts,&quot; Fidelity said in a statement.</p>
<p>Lloyd's of London has approved the Fidelity Institutional Cash Fund Plc, which has a triple A rating from Moody's and is quoted on the Dublin stock exchange, Fidelity said.</p>
<p>The minimum investment is $1.0 million.</p>
<p>Fidelity's UK operations are run by privately owned Fidelity Investments Ltd.</p>
<p>-- Reuters Insurance News 44 171 542 2769</p>
